    "teach_4": {
      "id": "teach_4",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Now the exam invents its own maths.\n\nIf * is an operation such that x * y = 3x + 2y, find 2 * 3 + 3 * 4.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_4_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_4_step": {
      "id": "teach_4_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The definition is a machine. Feed it numbers exactly as ordered:\n\n2 * 3 = 3 × 2 + 2 × 3 = 6 + 6 = 12\n3 * 4 = 3 × 3 + 2 × 4 = 9 + 8 = 17",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_4_step2"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_4_step2": {
      "id": "teach_4_step2",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Add the results:\n\n12 + 17 = 29\n\nThe order of feeding matters: x takes the first number, y the second. 2 * 3 and 3 * 2 are different.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_4"
        }
      ]
    },
